## Context
Split from 1311 at raid planning (2026-10-28; monster checklist: a TypeScript
extension, a projection entry and a live Pi control are their own sign-off
unit). 1311 ships Pi `wake` as an inbox writer: it writes a job into
`$IDH_WAKE_INBOX`, or answers NOOP "extension not loaded" when that is absent.
This child adds the reader.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `adapters/pi/extensions/idh-wake.ts`: at `session_start` (not in the factory)
      it creates the inbox, exports `IDH_WAKE_INBOX`, starts a timer, and delivers
      due jobs with `pi.sendUserMessage()` when idle
- [ ] Projection entry in `adapters/projections.json`, covered by `tests/test_adapter_deployment.py`
- [ ] Live controls on padme's local provider (no paid call): positive (an armed job
      starts a turn in an idle `pi`) and negative (no extension → exit 1 NOOP)
- [ ] `can wake.*` for Pi answers from the extension's presence; sitrep.md's Pi row updated
- [ ] `make check` passes
